comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:12:34.029Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for MCP 2026-07-28 conformance official schema protocol-era adapter Inspector real transport adversarial negative-control packed and published release gates. pm-kl11 and the current release probe only cover the obsolete initialize contract."
  "2026-08-25T05:18:50.346Z","harness:codex","Graph governance: removed four direct blocked_by rows that were already implied through typed leaf prerequisites. The release gate still waits for every MCP lane through pm-rzs24j, pm-hv1x1x, pm-8nzivt, pm-pznhee, and pm-vzcisw, while preserving the established redundancy ceiling."
  "2026-08-25T14:41:17.713Z","harness:codex","Progress evidence: added the official-revision owner matrix plus SDK helper and real-process stateless conformance coverage. PM-linked aggregate coverage, complete-tracker static assurance, and 12-test current-foundation cohort passed. The aggregate remains open because Streamable HTTP, tasks, cache/subscriptions, authorization/telemetry, deprecations, and published-consumer lanes retain separate active owners."
  "2026-08-25T15:01:38.183Z","harness:codex","Superseding current-foundation evidence: unversioned legacy requests carrying unrelated _meta remain on the compatibility adapter; strict modern validation activates only when protocolVersion is explicitly claimed. Focused foundation cohort is now 13 tests and the core PM-linked exact coverage/static suite passes on the corrected tree."
  "2026-08-26T15:49:44.799Z","harness:codex","Final conformance evidence: every declared prerequisite owner is live-verified closed with substantive resolution. Discovery, Skills, Apps, tasks, MRTR, cache/resource contracts, authorization, transport, subscriptions, deprecation inventory, release verifier, and real stateless process coverage converge on MCP 2026-07-28. Final exact coverage passed 583 files / 8,011 tests at 100/100/100/100; static quality and graph composition pass with zero canonical MCP deprecation violations; packed npx and bunx clients exercised discovery, four skills, five Apps, and App resource rendering."
  "2026-08-26T16:57:17.139Z","harness:codex","PR review remediation evidence: published verifier now requires the exact draft Skills revision/status, reads a listed skill resource, and independently verifies its SHA-256 digest for both text and binary payload paths. Structured fixtures cover wrong revision, wrong digest, and binary bunx success. Exact coverage and the full static/conformance gates passed; real packed npx and bunx MCP journeys returned five responses including discovery, Skills, Apps, app HTML, and digest-bearing skill content."
  "2026-08-26T17:43:07.566Z","harness:codex","Exact-head remediation evidence: the canonical protocol decision now documents implemented optional-Apps behavior precisely—incompatible declarations degrade tools/list and resources/list to non-UI discovery, while direct ui:// reads and every Skills method remain fail-closed. Focused conformance, deprecation inventory, static assurance, and exact coverage pass."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T15:49:43.255Z","harness:codex",Live publication proof is a post-merge operational claim. The reviewed source includes fail-closed npx/bunx stdio and HTTP verifier coverage; registry/tag verification will be recorded separately after the immutable release exists.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T14:41:18.438Z","harness:codex",Conformance links that execute repository governance must persist tracker context in the linked-test metadata so a plain pm test run is reproducible without operator-only overrides.
